Operational rule recorded with this card: do NOT run lane gate scripts and full `cargo test -p
lts-desktop --lib` concurrently — cargo does not serialize test EXECUTION across processes, so two
suites race the same whisper sidecar even though builds are lock-serialized. The in-process mutex
fixes the intra-suite race; cross-process overlap stays prohibited.

Wall-time note: the suite intentionally got slower (~6.5 min) because the 7 vendor-backed tests
serialize by design; that is the accepted cost of removing the flake class.

